{"id": "85863", "name": "CR-Diff-04-product-2.b", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p>Find the following derivative: \\[ \\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}[{{CT:1}}]. \\] [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>", "generalfeedback": "<p>In order to solve this problem we will have to use the product rule calc_product_rule as follows: \\[\\begin{array}{rcl}\\displaystyle \\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}[{{CT:1}}] &amp;\\displaystyle =&amp;\\displaystyle \\left[\\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}[{{CT:2}}]\\right]\\cdot {{CT:3}} + {{CT:2}}\\cdot \\left[\\frac{d}{d{{CT:0}}}[{{CT:3}}]\\right] \\\\ &amp;\\displaystyle =&amp;\\displaystyle {{CT:4}}\\cdot {{CT:3}} + {{CT:2}}\\cdot [{{CT:5}}] \\\\ &amp;\\displaystyle =&amp;\\displaystyle {{CT:6}} \\end{array}\\]</p>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Diff", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(p,v)", "testoptions": "v", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(pp1,v)*diff(pp2,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-1-T ", "feedback": "<p>To differentiate a product use the rule \\[\\frac{d}{dx}[fg] = \\frac{df}{dx}g+f\\frac{dg}{dx}.\\] You cannot get the derivative of a product by multiplying the derivatives.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "Result-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "diff(pp1,v)*pp1+pp2*diff(pp2,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-2-T ", "feedback": "<p>You appear to have applied the product rule incorrectly. It is \\[\\frac{df}{dx}g+f\\frac{dg}{dx},\\] not \\[f\\frac{df}{dx}+g\\frac{dg}{dx}.\\]</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "Result-2-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 3, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "-diff(pp1,v)*pp2-pp1*diff(pp2,v)", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-3-T ", "feedback": "<p>The derivative of \\(\\sin(mx)\\) is \\(m\\cos(mx)\\); you appear to have gained a minus sign which might suggest you have used \\(-m\\cos(mx)\\) as the derivative of \\(\\cos(mx)\\).</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-3-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["p", "pp1", "pp2", "rdm1", "rdm2", "v"], "nvariants": 24}